e simulated push; reset inside an applied push recovers that same commit, and a changed fork is refused. All 50 scripted workerd tests pass, including the original independently discovered external-effect windows, the 12 named resets, and SQLite conformance. One live-model test skipped deliberately. The compiler is now locally pinned and missing/failed compilers, own-file errors, configuration errors and changed vendor diagnostics fail. Seven check:test cases pass WITH root dependencies; standalone remains the P2 above. Dated author model result was read in full: 6 seconds, 2,191 tokens, one accepted claim/propose/land, no refusals, and the landing was accepted when the model claimed it had landed; Room's alarm later made it landed. This is author local-workerd/model evidence, not a checker deployment or live model run.\n\nCoverage: nine artifacts byte-identical to reviewed 0d7d9861; 18 revised/new artifacts examined, including source/tests/configs/scripts/docs and result records. Lock change only adds pinned TypeScript 7.0.2 and its platform-specific compiler packages; existing dependencies unchanged. /tmp/artroom-checker-pi2-byte-credit.json. All 21 inherited non-spike changes are byte-identical to approved main 4892e114. Source checkout clean. An extra local Wrangler dry bundle attempt is unsuccessful due to aliases selecting root Git exports; the committed wrangler config explicitly serves the test pool over fake remotes and is not a deployment delivery. Actual deployment, wiring and measurements remain open.\n\nArchitecture: durable signed intent and unresolved outcome belong to the Agent's storage while Room remains the authority. The outbox's lifetime now matches that distinction, and model prose is not treated as landing proof. Current code uses pinned older Room/client sources and a fake compare-and-swap workspace; it does not establish compatibility with the integrated current Room/real Git gateway. Security: the act bytes are replayed, not re-signed from 